OURS (not proposed to Guillaume Duboc). Printing only. to_quoted/2 prints a type whose
complement has fewer kinds (atoms, tuples, functions...) as the negation of that
complement: "term() minus a few tuples" reads not ({...} or {...}) instead of a union that
lists every other kind. The complement of the complement has more kinds, so this never
applies twice in a row and nothing is printed twice. In a closed tuple DNF line, a negated
tuple disjoint from the positive one is dropped, and one that contains it in every
component but one, k, is absorbed into that component:
{p1, ..., pn} and not {n1, ..., nn} = {p1, ..., pk and not nk, ..., pn}.
